<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ramesses II</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ramesses II was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">pharaoh</a> of the Nineteenth Dynasty of the Egyptian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-kingdom-of-egypt">New Kingdom</a>, who reigned for much of the thirteenth century BCE. He fought the Hittite king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muwatalli-ii">Muwatalli II</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-kadesh">Battle of Kadesh</a> in 1274 BCE and later concluded a peace treaty with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hittite-empire">Hittite Empire</a>. He is also known for monumental building projects such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-simbel">Abu Simbel</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ramesses-ii.jpg" alt="Ramesses II" width="280" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pbuergler · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ramses_II_British_Museum.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
